{
	"type": "root",
	"children": [
		{
			"type": "yaml",
			"value": "title: Deploying Next.js to different platforms\nnav_title: Deploying to Platforms\ndescription: Understand which Next.js features require specific platform capabilities and how to choose the right deployment target."
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Next.js "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "./rendering-philosophy.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "treats static and dynamic content as a spectrum"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " at the component level. Different features in this model require different platform capabilities. This page helps you understand what your platform needs to support and how to configure your deployment."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Minimum Requirements"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "To run Next.js, your platform needs "
				},
				{
					"type": "strong",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "a Node.js server"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ". That's it."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "A single "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "next start"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " process handles every Next.js feature correctly: Server Components, ISR, PPR, Cache Components, Server Actions, Proxy, and "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "after()"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ". Streaming support is needed for features like PPR and Server Components to deliver content progressively (without it, responses are buffered and sent as a whole, which still works but loses the streaming performance benefit). Additional infrastructure (CDN caching, edge compute, shared cache) primarily improves performance and multi-instance consistency. In multi-instance deployments, shared cache and tag coordination reduce stale divergence between instances. The only additional dependency is the "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "sharp"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " package, which is required for "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "../03-api-reference/02-components/image.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Image Optimization"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Functional Fidelity vs. Performance Fidelity"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "When evaluating platform support for Next.js, it helps to distinguish between two levels:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "strong",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Functional fidelity"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " means every Next.js feature works correctly. The "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "../03-api-reference/07-adapters/04-testing-adapters.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "adapter test suite"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " is the contract: if a platform's adapter passes the tests, it supports Next.js. This is binary: it passes or it doesn't."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "strong",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Performance fidelity"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " means features achieve their optimal performance characteristics. Examples include PPR's static shell served at CDN latency rather than origin latency, or ISR serving stale content instantly with sub-second revalidation propagation. Performance fidelity is a spectrum that every platform will achieve differently based on their architecture."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "A platform that achieves functional fidelity is a fully supported deployment target for Next.js. Performance fidelity is how platforms differentiate, and it improves incrementally over time."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Use the feature matrix below through this lens: \"Streaming Required\" and \"Shared Cache Recommended\" describe what is needed for functional fidelity. \"Edge Stitching\" is a performance fidelity optimization."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Feature Support Matrix"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Different features require different infrastructure capabilities. The \"Edge Stitching\" column is a "
				},
				{
					"type": "strong",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "performance optimization"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ", not a correctness requirement. All features work correctly from a single origin server."
				}
			]
		},
