		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "These are available building blocks, not finished integrations. Most community adapters today deploy Next.js as a Docker container or Node.js server without leveraging CDN-specific primitives like edge KV or PPR resuming. See the "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "../01-getting-started/17-deploying.md#adapters",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Deploying"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " page for the current list of adapters. For CDN-specific caching considerations (including known limitations with "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "Vary"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " on custom headers), see "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "./cdn-caching.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "CDN Caching"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Adapters"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Next.js provides a "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "../03-api-reference/05-config/01-next-config-js/adapterPath.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Deployment Adapter API"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " that lets platforms customize how Next.js applications are built and deployed for their infrastructure. Adapters run at build time and produce platform-specific output from the standard Next.js build. Anyone can build an adapter using the public API with no special access required."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "The adapter API plus Next.js caching interfaces form the complete platform integration surface. The adapter handles build-time output, while "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "cacheHandler"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " and "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "cacheHandlers"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " cover different runtime caching paths. "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "cacheHandler"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " (singular) covers server cache paths like ISR, route handlers, patched "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "fetch"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "/"
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "unstable_cache"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ", and image optimization. "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "cacheHandlers"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " (plural) configures "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "'use cache'"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " directive backends."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 3,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Verified Adapters"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "A "
				},
				{
					"type": "strong",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "verified adapter"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " is one that meets two requirements:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "list",
			"ordered": true,
			"start": 1,
			"spread": false,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "strong",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "text",
											"value": "Open source."
										}
									]
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " The adapter source code is publicly available so the community and the Next.js team can inspect, contribute to, and verify it."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "strong",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "text",
											"value": "Runs the compatibility test suite."
										}
									]
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " The platform provides a way to run the full "
								},
								{
									"type": "link",
									"title": null,
									"url": "../03-api-reference/07-adapters/04-testing-adapters.md",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "text",
											"value": "Next.js compatibility test suite"
										}
									]
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " against their adapter. This gives visibility into which features work, which are in progress, and where gaps remain."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Verified adapters are hosted under the "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "https://github.com/nextjs",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Next.js GitHub organization"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ", listed as supported deployment targets in the Next.js documentation, and maintained by their respective platform teams. There are no private framework hooks or integration paths: Vercel's adapter uses the same public API as every other adapter."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "For verified adapters and platforms working toward verified status through the "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "https://nextjs.org/ecosystem-working-group",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Ecosystem Working Group"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ", the Next.js team commits to:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "list",
			"ordered": false,
			"start": null,
			"spread": false,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "strong",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "text",
											"value": "Coordinated testing."
										}
									]
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " Before major releases, we work with platform teams to run the compatibility test suite and surface issues early."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "strong",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "text",
											"value": "Early access."
										}
									]
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " Adapter authors receive early access to API changes during RFCs and release candidates."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "strong",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "text",
											"value": "Direct support."
										}
									]
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " When the adapter contract needs updating, we work directly with adapter teams."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "blockquote",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "paragraph",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "strong",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "Good to know:"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " Platforms can build closed-source adapters on the same public API and test suite. However, closed-source adapters will not be listed as verified, since the Next.js team cannot verify what it cannot inspect."
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "A Note on Infrastructure Requirements"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Next.js's "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "./rendering-philosophy.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "rendering model"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " places the static/dynamic boundary at the component level rather than the route level. Finer-grained boundaries provide more flexibility for developers at the cost of broader requirements for hosting platforms. This is a deliberate trade-off: the infrastructure requirements on this page exist because of what the rendering model delivers."
				}
			]
		},
		{
